# The Act 1 midpoint report, the road out, and the Act 1 end scene.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2849–2900.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/ch2_ending.tscn.
# The report seeds faction reputation (Hearth / Archive / Continuity); it is
# not the Axis 2 lock. The road sets Act 1's pace (early / on time / late).

~ report
Kaelen (Internal): Two fragments, the tower logs, what was under the market. Right now the only copy is in my head. Somebody else should hold a backup.
? Kaelen (Internal): Who gets the copy?
- The councils, Oakhaven's and Ironhold's. They're the ones who'll live with whatever it means. => report_local
- The archivists in the Wastes. If anyone out there keeps records properly, it's them. => report_archive
- Ironhold command. They're the ones who can act on it tomorrow. => report_command

~ report_local
set act1_report_local
[if has_elara] Elara: Mara will read every word of that over breakfast, then tell the whole lane it was her idea.

~ report_archive
set act1_report_archive
Kaelen (Internal): Somebody out there writes things down for a living. Bran would like them. I hope they're honest about it.

~ report_command
set act1_report_command
Brask: I'll read it. I might even agree with some of it.

~ road_out
Kaelen (Internal): The next trace points at the Fractured Wastes.
[if ch2_seraphina_recruited] Seraphina: Three roads. The safe one's long. The old server road's short, and I wouldn't march a wagon down it. The caravan needs Oakhaven's bridge.
[if not ch2_seraphina_recruited] Rook: Three roads to the Wastes, priced for you: long and safe, short and stupid, or the caravan, if Oakhaven's bridge is still up.
[if ch1_bridge_fell] Kaelen (Internal): It isn't. That leaves two roads.
? Kaelen (Internal): Which way out?
- The old server road. Fast, if the ground stays under us. It's unstable. => pace_early
- The safe road. Long gets there too. => pace_on_time
- [if not ch1_bridge_fell] The caravan route. Ride with the traders. => pace_late

~ pace_early
set act1_pace_early

~ pace_on_time
set act1_pace_on_time

~ pace_late
set act1_pace_late
Rook: Caravan leaves at noon, and I'm on it. You're paying for your own cart. It isn't cheap; I know the man who owns it.

# The Act 1 end scene, on Ironhold's outer bridge.
~ end
[if ch2_seraphina_recruited] => end_recruited
[if ch2_seraphina_stayed] => end_stayed
[if ch2_seraphina_rejected] => end_rejected
=> end_horizon

~ end_recruited
do seraphina_joins
Seraphina: My banner's folded in your pack. Don't use it as a pillow.
=> end_horizon

~ end_stayed
Seraphina: Bring me back something useful, please. Not stories. I get stories off every wagon through that gate.
Kaelen: Useful like what? A map? A spare part? I'm terrible at gifts.
Seraphina: Answers. The kind I can put in a report and Brask can't send back.
Kaelen: Those are rare out here. I'll look under everything.
Seraphina: Then bring coffee. And this time drink it. Don't wear it.
=> end_horizon

~ end_rejected
Seraphina: I hope I'm wrong about you.
Kaelen: Me too. I'd— I'd like you to be.
Elara: She counted you on the way out, you know. Habit. Come on, the road's long.
Kaelen: I know. I'm keeping that.
=> end_horizon

~ end_horizon
[if ch1_bridge_fell] Kaelen (Internal): A refugee wagon's coming up the Oakhaven road, loaded to the rails. That'll be the bridge.
[if ch1_bridge_saved] Kaelen (Internal): A trade wagon's heading down toward Oakhaven. It'll cross on mismatched planks, and they'll hold.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Kaelen (Internal): The infirmary bells are still going. Tomas. The Wren girl.
[if ch2_medicine_early] Kaelen (Internal): Every light in the lower city is on. Rem's got beds to spare tonight.
do sky_seam
Kaelen: That way. Past the hills.
Elara: You say that like the sky's pointing.
Kaelen: It is. You've watched me check it every few steps since Oakhaven.
